## Former blocker P4-B01: closed

**Disposition: PASS.**

`SceneCommands.h:579-584` declares the required atomic
`setCameraFromView(CameraId, NodeId, CameraProperties, NodeTransform, guard)`
surface. `SceneCommands.cpp:6276` implements it as exactly one
`mutate(..., HistoryPolicy::nonHistory, ...)` transaction. Before candidate
mutation it validates guard, camera authority/liveness, node
authority/liveness, camera properties, finite transform components, and
normalized rotation. It applies camera and transform to one candidate and
publishes that candidate once.

`scene_commands_tests.cpp:1751-1891` proves:

- combined camera plus transform change publishes one revision;
- camera-only and transform-only changes each publish one revision;
- exact combined equality is the only no-op and leaves revision/history intact;
- invalid camera leaves the requested transform untouched;
- invalid transform leaves the requested camera untouched;
- stale revision, stale token, foreign camera, foreign node, stale camera, and
  stale node all reject atomically;
- document identity, revision, token, all object records, and complete history
  state remain unchanged on every rejected path.

The same test executable passed directly in both Debug and Release/NDEBUG and
inside both full CTest matrices. B01 is closed by production plus executable
failure-atomicity evidence, not by repair prose.

